Original commit body from 58861a0:

Add a `changes` job that detects if code files changed. Jobs that
only make sense for code changes (lint, audit, verify-generated,
pytest) now depend on this and skip when only docs changed.

Docs-only patterns that skip expensive jobs:
- *.md files
- LICENSE, .gitignore, etc.

Jobs that always run:
- changes (detection job)
- dco (sign-off still required for all PRs)

This saves ~6 minutes of CI time for documentation PRs.
